Anycast DNS for Global Speed & High Availability
In advanced scale designs, you shouldn't use traditional single-location Unicast routing. You use Anycast DNS, where multiple authoritative servers around the globe all advertise the exact same IP address using Border Gateway Protocol (BGP). The internet’s core routers automatically send the user’s request to the topologically nearest server node, slashing latency and absorbing massive DDoS attacks naturally.

DNS Cache Poisoning / Spoofing
This occurs when an attacker exploits vulnerabilities in UDP communication to inject a fraudulent IP record into a recursive resolver's cache entry. The resolver then blindly redirects legitimate users to a phishing website until the TTL expires.
solution: The Industry Defense: the architecture enforces DNSSEC (Domain Name System Security Extensions), which adds cryptographic digital signatures to records to prove authenticity before caching them.

Flushing Cache
during a production issue, in Windows, this is achieved using ipconfig /flushdns in the command prompt, while macOS utilizes sudo killall -HUP mDNSResponder loops.